---
import CarbonLayout from "../layouts/CarbonLayout.astro";
import AOSInit from "../components/AOSInit.astro";

export const prerender = true;
---

<CarbonLayout title="About USRad - The Full Story" isHeroPage={false}>
  <AOSInit />

  <!-- Hero Section with Background Image -->
  <section
    class="relative pt-32 pb-20 px-4 sm:px-6 min-h-[600px] flex items-center"
  >
    <!-- Background Image -->
    <div class="absolute inset-0 z-0">
      <img
        src="/images/about-hero-f.webp"
        alt="Worker with family"
        class="w-full h-full object-cover"
      />
      <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-r from-black/70 to-black/40">
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Content -->
    <div class="relative z-10 max-w-7xl mx-auto">
      <div class="max-w-5xl">
        <h1 class="mb-8" data-aos="fade-up">
          <span
            class="block text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-medium text-white/80 tracking-wide mb-3"
          >
            The Story Behind
          </span>
          <span
            class="block text-7xl sm:text-8xl md:text-9xl font-bold text-[#B08A4A] leading-none tracking-tight"
          >
            USRad
          </span>
        </h1>
        <p
          class="text-xl md:text-2xl text-gray-100 leading-relaxed max-w-2xl mb-4"
          data-aos="fade-up"
          data-aos-delay="200"
        >
          One price for the study, with the radiologist&rsquo;s interpretation
          included.
        </p>
        <p
          class="text-base md:text-lg text-[#B08A4A] font-medium tracking-wide max-w-2xl"
          data-aos="fade-up"
          data-aos-delay="300"
        >
          We&rsquo;re building the category of Accessible Imaging.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Founders Documentary Hero -->
  <section
    id="founders-photo"
    class="py-16 px-4 sm:px-6 bg-white border-b border-gray-100"
  >
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto">
      <!-- Documentary Label -->
      <div class="mb-10" data-aos="fade-up">
        <p
          class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[#B08A4A]"
        >
          1994 &mdash; The Founding Moment
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-0 items-stretch min-h-[580px]">
        <!-- Left: Founders Photo -->
        <div class="relative flex flex-col" data-aos="fade-right">
          <figure class="flex-1 flex flex-col">
            <div class="flex-1 overflow-hidden rounded-md shadow-md">
              <img
                src="/images/founders_restored.webp"
                alt="Michael and Donna Cabrera inside a diagnostic imaging center, mid-1990s"
                class="w-full h-full object-cover object-[center_15%]"
                loading="eager"
                width="1000"
                height="1300"
              />
            </div>
            <figcaption class="mt-4 pl-1">
              <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <div class="w-px h-10 bg-[#cc9933] flex-shrink-0 mt-1"></div>
                <div>
                  <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 tracking-wide">
                    Michael &amp; Donna Cabrera
                  </p>
                  <p
                    class="text-xs text-gray-400 mt-0.5 tracking-wider uppercase"
                  >
                    Diagnostic imaging center &mdash; mid-1990s
                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>
            </figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>

        <!-- Right: Headline + Narrative -->
        <div
          class="flex flex-col justify-center md:pl-16 pt-10 md:pt-0"
          data-aos="fade-left"
          data-aos-delay="150"
        >
          <p
            class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-[#cc9933] mb-5"
          >
            The Origin
          </p>

          <h2
            class="text-4xl md:text-5xl lg:text-6xl font-bold text-gray-900 leading-tight mb-6"
          >
            Where It All<br />
            <span class="text-[#003087]">Started.</span>
          </h2>

          <div class="space-y-5 text-lg text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
            <p>
              In the early 1990s, imaging centers had open capacity and injured
              workers couldn&rsquo;t reach it. Authorization ran through
              carriers by fax and phone. Most facilities wouldn&rsquo;t schedule
              until someone approved. Nobody in the chain was accountable for
              how long it took.
            </p>
            <p>
              Florida workers&rsquo; compensation law let employers direct care.
              So in 1994, Michael and Donna Cabrera founded Managed Care
              Networks, Inc., operating as AnciCare PPO &mdash; a specialty
              preferred provider organization delivering medical imaging through
              a contracted network of independent diagnostic facilities. Volume
              commitments to imaging centers in exchange for rates below the fee
              schedule, and one party accountable for scheduling.
            </p>
            <p>
              AnciCare sold to insurers, third-party administrators and
              self-insured employers. The business was focused on workers&rsquo;
              compensation, while also accepting referrals from auto liability
              and group health.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- The Origin Story -->
  <section class="py-20 px-4 sm:px-6 bg-white">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto">
      <!-- ACT 3 — THE DOCUMENTED RECORD. Rebuilt 2026-08-17 as a single-column historical record. The former two-column layout paired a narrative that duplicated Act 2 with a four-tile credibility panel whose tiles were all defective: a founder-career span under an AnciCare heading (#27), an unanchored facility count (rule 18), a barred savings figure (§6) and a barred people-count (§4b/§4c). Its footer carried the D3 priority claim. ⛔ PROSE, NOT TILES, BY RULING — a dated facility count in a bare tile sheds its date and migrates to the present, which is how an unanchored count became a USRad network claim on the homepage. All figures below are §4a-registered, most admitted 2026-08-16. The historical savings percentage is omitted by founder ruling 2026-08-15 to avoid conflation with the separately governed present-day MRI claim at §1d. The "Read the essay" link to /blog/the-scan-that-never-happens is removed: verified 2026-08-17 that the destination still publishes a barred savings figure at :306, plus an unanchored facility count, a barred people-count and a D3 priority claim. /blog is a queued surface with open items #65, #73, #74 and #75, none scheduled. ⛔ THE LINK MAY RETURN ONCE THE DESTINATION IS REMEDIATED. -->
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto" data-aos="fade-up">
        <p
          class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[#B08A4A] mb-4"
        >
          The AnciCare Record &middot; 1994&ndash;2002
        </p>
        <h2 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">
          What They Built
        </h2>

        <div
          class="h-px w-24 bg-gradient-to-r from-[#cc9933] to-transparent mb-8"
        >
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-6 text-lg text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
          <p>
            AnciCare grew from a South Florida program into a national
            contracting operation. At the end of 1998 it held 608 imaging
            facilities across 32 states and the District of Columbia. By April
            2002 it had 1,228 contracted imaging facilities across 43 states.
          </p>

          <p>
            The operating volume was real, not projected. From 1994 through
            2001, AnciCare paid more than $60 million to imaging centers &mdash;
            money that moved through the network to the facilities doing the
            work.
          </p>

          <p>
            Speed was the operating advantage. In February 1999 the
            <em>South Florida Business Journal</em> reported that 90% of AnciCare&rsquo;s
            referrals were scheduled within two to three days.
          </p>

          <p>
            The customers included insurers, third-party administrators and
            self-insured employers. Winn-Dixie, CNA, Liberty Mutual, Zurich
            American, USF&amp;G, Crawford &amp; Company, Gallagher &amp; Bassett
            and the U.S. Postal Service were among them.
          </p>

          <p>
            Independent recognition followed: #210 on the 1999
            <em>Inc.</em> 500; No. 1 on the
            <em>South Florida Business Journal</em>&rsquo;s 1999 list of South
            Florida&rsquo;s largest PPOs; and recognition by
            <em>Hispanic Business</em> among the nation&rsquo;s 500 largest Hispanic-owned
            companies.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- REVOLUTIONARY TIMELINE SECTION -->
  <section
    id="timeline"
    class="relative py-32 bg-gradient-to-b from-gray-900 via-gray-800 to-gray-900 overflow-hidden"
  >
    <!-- Animated Background -->
    <div class="absolute inset-0">
      <div
        class="absolute inset-0 bg-[url('data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg width="
        60"
        height="60"
        viewBox="0 0 60 60"
        xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
        %3E%3Cg
        fill="none"
        fill-rule="evenodd"
        %3E%3Cg
        fill="%239C92AC"
        fill-opacity="0.03"
        %3E%3Cpath
        d="M36 34v-4h-2v4h-4v2h4v4h2v-4h4v-2h-4zm0-30V0h-2v4h-4v2h4v4h2V6h4V4h-4zM6 34v-4H4v4H0v2h4v4h2v-4h4v-2H6zM6 4V0H4v4H0v2h4v4h2V6h4V4H6z"
        %3E%3C
        g%3E%3C
        g%3E%3C
        svg%3E')]
        opacity-20"
      >
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="relative z-10 max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6">
      <!-- Section Header -->
      <div class="text-center mb-20" data-aos="fade-up">
        <div
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-3 bg-white/10 backdrop-blur-sm px-6 py-3 rounded-full mb-8"
        >
          <div class="w-2 h-2 bg-[#cc9933] rounded-full animate-pulse"></div>
          <span
            class="text-white/80 text-sm font-medium tracking-wider uppercase"
            >The Timeline</span
          >
          <div class="w-2 h-2 bg-[#003087] rounded-full animate-pulse"></div>
        </div>
        <h2 class="text-5xl md:text-6xl lg:text-7xl font-bold text-white mb-6">
          Two Companies.<br />
          <span
            class="bg-gradient-to-r from-[#cc9933] to-[#003087] bg-clip-text text-transparent"
            >Two Eras.</span
          >
        </h2>
        <p class="text-lg text-white/50 max-w-xl mx-auto mt-4">
          AnciCare ended with its 2002 acquisition. Work on today&rsquo;s USRad
          began in 2025.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- The Timeline — TWO ERAS, TWO PATHS.
           The AnciCare path terminates at the May 2002 acquisition. The USRad
           path starts separately in 2025. The 23-year span between them is
           deliberately empty: no copy, no marker, no connective element.
           The gap IS the statement (founder ruling, Act 4). -->

      <!-- ERA LABEL: AnciCare -->
      <div class="flex justify-center mb-12" data-aos="fade-up">
        <div
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-3 bg-white/5 border border-[#cc9933]/40 backdrop-blur-sm px-5 py-2 rounded-full"
        >
          <div class="w-2 h-2 bg-[#cc9933] rounded-full"></div>
          <span
            class="text-white/70 text-xs sm:text-sm font-medium tracking-[0.2em] uppercase"
            >AnciCare &middot; 1994&ndash;2002</span
          >
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- ANCICARE ERA PATH (gold) -->
      <div class="relative pb-24">
        <!-- Center Path — gold, solid to its end. No fade-out: this era stops. -->
        <div
          class="absolute left-1/2 top-0 bottom-0 w-0.5 transform -translate-x-1/2"
          style="background: linear-gradient(to bottom, transparent, rgba(176,138,74,0.6) 12%, rgba(176,138,74,0.6) 100%);"
        >
        </div>
        <!-- Full stop. The AnciCare era ends at the 2002 acquisition. -->
        <div
          class="timeline-cap absolute left-1/2 bottom-0 w-10 h-1 bg-[#cc9933] rounded-full transform -translate-x-1/2"
        >
        </div>

        <!-- 1993: The Discovery — ACT 1 ANCHOR -->
        <div class="relative flex items-center mb-32" data-aos="fade-right">
          <div class="w-full md:w-1/2 text-right pr-8 md:pr-16">
            <div class="inline-block">
              <span
                class="text-[#cc9933] text-8xl md:text-9xl font-bold opacity-60"
                >1993</span
              >
              <h3 class="text-3xl font-bold text-white mt-4 mb-3">
                The Discovery
              </h3>
              <p class="text-gray-300 text-lg max-w-md ml-auto">
                Imaging centers had open capacity. Injured workers
                couldn&rsquo;t reach it.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="absolute left-1/2 transform -translate-x-1/2 z-10">
            <div
              class="w-24 h-24 bg-gray-900 rounded-full border-4 border-[#cc9933] flex items-center justify-center group hover:bg-gray-800 transition-all duration-300"
            >
              <img
                src="/images/icons/magnifying-glass.svg"
                alt="Discovery"
                class="w-12 h-12 filter-gold group-hover:scale-110 transition-transform duration-300"
              />
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="hidden md:block w-1/2"></div>
        </div>

        <!-- 1994: AnciCare Launch — ACT 1 ANCHOR -->
        <div class="relative flex items-center mb-32" data-aos="fade-left">
          <div class="hidden md:block w-1/2"></div>
          <div class="absolute left-1/2 transform -translate-x-1/2 z-10">
            <div
              class="w-24 h-24 bg-gray-900 rounded-full border-4 border-[#cc9933] flex items-center justify-center group hover:bg-gray-800 transition-all duration-300"
            >
              <img
                src="/images/icons/social.svg"
                alt="Network Launch"
                class="w-12 h-12 filter-gold group-hover:scale-110 transition-transform duration-300"
              />
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="w-full md:w-1/2 pl-8 md:pl-16">
            <span
              class="text-[#cc9933] text-8xl md:text-9xl font-bold opacity-60"
              >1994</span
            >
            <h3 class="text-3xl font-bold text-white mt-4 mb-3">
              AnciCare Launches
            </h3>
            <p class="text-gray-300 text-lg max-w-md">
              Direct contracts. Volume commitments in exchange for rates below
              the fee schedule.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- 1999: Scale — supporting year, visually subdued -->
        <div class="relative flex items-center mb-24" data-aos="fade-right">
          <div class="w-full md:w-1/2 text-right pr-8 md:pr-16">
            <div class="inline-block opacity-70">
              <span class="text-[#cc9933]/40 text-5xl md:text-6xl font-bold"
                >1999</span
              >
              <h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-white/80 mt-3 mb-2">
                National Expansion
              </h3>
              <p class="text-gray-400 text-base max-w-md ml-auto">
                Expansion beyond Florida. Employers and carriers on board.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="absolute left-1/2 transform -translate-x-1/2 z-10">
            <div
              class="w-24 h-24 bg-gray-900 rounded-full border-4 border-[#cc9933] flex items-center justify-center group hover:bg-gray-800 transition-all duration-300"
            >
              <img
                src="/images/icons/increase.svg"
                alt="Explosive Growth"
                class="w-12 h-12 filter-gold group-hover:scale-110 transition-transform duration-300"
              />
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="hidden md:block w-1/2"></div>
        </div>

        <!-- 2002: The Exit — ANCICARE ERA ANCHOR.
             Full-weight treatment matching 1993 and 1994. The acquisition is
             the strongest documented fact on this page and is styled as such. -->
        <div class="relative flex items-center" data-aos="fade-left">
          <div class="hidden md:block w-1/2"></div>
          <div class="absolute left-1/2 transform -translate-x-1/2 z-10">
            <div
              class="w-24 h-24 bg-gray-900 rounded-full border-4 border-[#cc9933] flex items-center justify-center group hover:bg-gray-800 transition-all duration-300"
            >
              <img
                src="/images/icons/hand-shake.svg"
                alt="Mission Accomplished"
                class="w-12 h-12 filter-gold group-hover:scale-110 transition-transform duration-300"
              />
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="w-full md:w-1/2 pl-8 md:pl-16">
            <span
              class="text-[#cc9933] text-8xl md:text-9xl font-bold opacity-60"
              >2002</span
            >
            <h3 class="text-3xl font-bold text-white mt-4 mb-3">
              AnciCare Is Acquired
            </h3>
            <p class="text-gray-300 text-lg max-w-md">
              CorVel Corporation (NASDAQ: CRVL) acquired AnciCare in May 2002.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <!-- THE 23-YEAR INTERVAL. Intentionally empty. Do not fill this.
           No copy, no marker, no animated element, no "meanwhile". -->
      <div class="h-40 md:h-64" aria-hidden="true"></div>

      <!-- ERA LABEL: USRad -->
      <div class="flex justify-center mb-12" data-aos="fade-up">
        <div
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-3 bg-white/5 border border-[#3b72d9]/50 backdrop-blur-sm px-5 py-2 rounded-full"
        >
          <div class="w-2 h-2 bg-[#3b72d9] rounded-full"></div>
          <span
            class="text-white/70 text-xs sm:text-sm font-medium tracking-[0.2em] uppercase"
            >USRad &middot; 2025&ndash;</span
          >
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- USRAD ERA PATH (blue) — a separate path, not a continuation.
           #3b72d9 is #003087 lifted for legibility on the dark gradient,
           the same way the gold path uses a muted #cc9933. -->
      <div class="relative pb-8">
        <!-- Hard start. This path begins in 2025; it does not arrive from above. -->
        <div
          class="timeline-cap absolute left-1/2 top-0 w-10 h-1 bg-[#3b72d9] rounded-full transform -translate-x-1/2"
        >
        </div>
        <div
          class="absolute left-1/2 top-0 bottom-0 w-0.5 transform -translate-x-1/2"
          style="background: linear-gradient(to bottom, rgba(59,114,217,0.7) 0%, rgba(59,114,217,0.7) 60%, transparent 100%);"
        >
        </div>

        <!-- 2025: USRad Born — ACT 3 ANCHOR, dramatic reveal -->
        <div class="relative flex items-center pt-16" data-aos="fade-right">
          <div class="w-full md:w-1/2 text-right pr-8 md:pr-16">
            <div class="inline-block">
              <span class="text-white text-8xl md:text-9xl font-bold opacity-80"
                >2025</span
              >
              <h3 class="text-3xl font-bold text-white mt-4 mb-3">
                The Work Begins
              </h3>
              <p class="text-gray-300 text-lg max-w-md ml-auto">
                Work begins on today&rsquo;s USRad, built for self-funded health
                plans and people paying directly for their own imaging.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="absolute left-1/2 transform -translate-x-1/2 z-10">
            <div
              class="w-24 h-24 bg-gray-900 rounded-full border-4 border-[#003087] flex items-center justify-center animate-pulse overflow-hidden p-4 hover:bg-gray-800 transition-all duration-300"
            >
              <img
                src="/images/logo/brand/usrad-pin.svg"
                alt="USRad Logo"
                class="w-full h-full object-contain"
              />
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="hidden md:block w-1/2"></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <style>
    /* Add smooth scroll behavior */
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
      .timeline-node {
        transition: all 0.8s cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1);
      }
    }

    /* Enhanced hover effects for timeline nodes */
    .group:hover {
      box-shadow: 0 0 30px rgba(204, 153, 51, 0.3);
    }

    /* USRad era nodes */
    .border-[#003087].group:hover {
      box-shadow: 0 0 30px rgba(0, 48, 135, 0.3);
    }

    /* CSS filter for gold color #cc9933 */
    .filter-gold {
      filter: brightness(0) saturate(100%) invert(79%) sepia(50%)
        saturate(1500%) hue-rotate(359deg) brightness(1.1) contrast(0.9);
    }

    /* CSS filter for white color */
    .filter-white {
      filter: brightness(0) invert(1);
    }

    /* Mobile adjustments */
    @media (max-width: 768px) {
      /* Stack timeline rows vertically */
      .relative.flex.items-center {
        flex-direction: column !important;
        align-items: flex-start !important;
      }

      /* Pull icon out of absolute positioning on mobile so it flows in the column */
      .relative.flex.items-center > .absolute.left-1\/2 {
        position: relative !important;
        left: auto !important;
        transform: none !important;
        margin-bottom: 1rem;
        order: -1; /* Icon always appears first */
      }

      /* Content blocks take full width */
      .relative.flex.items-center > div[class*="w-full"] {
        width: 100% !important;
        padding-left: 0 !important;
        padding-right: 0 !important;
      }

      .text-right {
        text-align: left !important;
      }

      .ml-auto {
        margin-left: 0 !important;
      }

      .pr-8,
      .pl-8 {
        padding: 0 !important;
      }

      /* Center line: shift to left edge on mobile for cleaner look.
       Applies to both era paths — each carries left-1/2 top-0 bottom-0. */
      #timeline .absolute.left-1\/2.top-0.bottom-0 {
        left: 2rem !important;
        transform: none !important;
      }

      /* Era path terminators follow their line to the left rail on mobile.
       These are NOT matched by the rule above (each has only one of
       top-0 / bottom-0), so they need their own shift. */
      #timeline .timeline-cap {
        left: 2rem !important;
        transform: translateX(-50%) !important;
      }
    }
  </style>

  <!-- Section wrapper. The retired case study this section was named for was DELETED 2026-08-17 (About step 1, founder-ruled); git baseline 411577a is the preservation record. id="case-study-246m" retired with it — retaining it would have emitted trust_content_view with section=case_study_246m for unrelated surviving content. Surviving children: the Next Era pillars, the founder promise, the founders section and the final CTA. Wrapper classes retained pending Act 6 composition review. -->
  <section
    class="py-24 px-4 sm:px-6 bg-gradient-to-br from-white to-gray-50 overflow-hidden"
  >
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto">
      <!-- THE NEXT ERA: Mission Pillars -->
      <div class="relative overflow-hidden bg-white">
        <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto py-24 px-6">
          <!-- ACT 5 — THE FIREWALL. Replaces the former "The Next Era / This Time, It's Different" block and its three mission pillars, 2026-08-17. Removed: the "Built on Experience" pillar (A→C transfer, rule 26, and an unanchored facility count under rule 18); the "No Permission Required" pillar (founder ruling 2026-08-16 — MRI requires a physician order); and the Direct to Patients pillar (dropped by ruling, not relocated). This section states the corporate and operational inheritance boundary: the founders' experience carries forward, AnciCare's network, contracts, clients and assets do not. ⛔ PARAGRAPHS 2 AND 3 ARE LOAD-BEARING AS A PAIR — the concession "That part is familiar" is safe only because the next paragraph immediately corrects it. Do not separate them with a divider, card treatment or oversized spacing. -->
          <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
            <!-- Chapter label + headline -->
            <div class="text-center mb-12" data-aos="fade-up">
              <p
                class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[#B08A4A] mb-5"
              >
                2025 &mdash; A New Company
              </p>
              <h2
                class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6 leading-tight"
              >
                What Carries Forward. What Doesn&rsquo;t.
              </h2>
              <div class="h-0.5 w-16 bg-[#B08A4A] mx-auto mt-2 opacity-60">
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- The firewall -->
            <div class="space-y-6 text-lg text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-16">
              <p data-aos="fade-up">
                USRad is a new company. It did not inherit AnciCare&rsquo;s
                network, contracts, clients or operating assets.
              </p>
              <p data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="100">
                What carries forward are the founders and what they learned
                building a contracted imaging network: working directly with
                independent imaging centers, establishing predictable pricing
